RUN AS THE SKILL (root-cause, fetched fresh), 2026-10-02, triaging art:vscode-call-door-field-report-2026-10-02, limitation 17, under rule:field-feedback-issues-are-root-caused-and-ideas-are-brainstormed. Triage agent C, dev_reflow2 hub.

① OBSERVED, the reporter's words: "a call refused on a later check (a link's arguments, a property enum) had already stored the node body; the corrected call then reported 'already held' or replaced a prior value. Import is atomic; typed writers are not." EXPECTED: a refused call writes nothing. NOT AFFECTED: import_graph, create_nodes/create_edges, draw_edges (they use the core's atomic batch).

② PRECEDENT: searched on the raw words. No earlier finding. dec:bulk-is-all-or-nothing-with-per-item-findings (accepted) already says "a partial bulk write leaves a design in a state nobody chose" and names the store's atomic batch (begin_batch/commit_batch/discard_batch), but scopes it to bulk forms.

③④⑤ MEASURED with reflow2-mcp 0.77.0 --call on a scratch store (log: /home/ajs7/.claude/jobs/fa666a94/tmp/triage-C/measure.log). Each case was refused (exit 1), then read back with get_node.
NODE LEFT BEHIND, 13 constructors:
- add_requirement (priority 'urgent-ish');
- add_capability (tier);
- add_component (tier);
- add_constraint (priority);
- add_flow (tier);
- add_actor (actor_type);
- add_project (status);
- add_artifact (status);
- add_release (status);
- add_epoch (status);
- add_verification (status; and a VERIFIES target of the wrong type, a Decision);
- add_decision (kind 'exploratry'; a related_to item naming a missing id; relation RELATES_TO);
- record_finding (caused_by naming a missing id).
NO NODE LEFT: add_capability with a bad status, add_verification with a bad method or missing target, add_change_event, record_finding with bad steps or basis, and anything refused at deserialisation (missing evidence on a link item).
THE SPLIT: a value checked by the core constructor itself, or before it, is atomic. A value written by a later upsert is not: set_optional_props, the kind upsert, review_relations, g.verifies, set_verification_status, the CAUSES edge.
None of the refusals said the node was stored.

WORSE THAN REPORTED, three ways.
(a) A FALSE "NOTHING WAS WRITTEN". add_capability on an EXISTING id with a new description and satisfies naming a missing requirement: the refusal says "the thread cannot be drawn and nothing was written". get_node shows the description rewritten. The hand-rolled rollback is guarded by !existed, so a revise keeps the overwrite.
(b) THE RETRY SKIPS THE DUPLICATE GUARD. search_first returns None when the id already existed (a revise). add_decision checks `kind` BEFORE the duplicate guard. Measured: a near-duplicate exploratory idea with kind 'Exploratory' was refused on kind and stored. The corrected retry landed as a "revision", with no duplicate refusal and no relatedness refusal. The control, the same text with a valid kind, was refused as a near-duplicate.
(c) THE LEFTOVER BLOCKS THE NEXT WRITE. A half-stored dec:probe-link became the near-match that refused the next, different decision.

⑥ THE CLASS: atomicity is a property of the bulk door only. The core's batch is pub(crate), so the MCP layer reaches it only through DesignGraph::atomically over a list of items. Each typed handler is a sequence of individually durable upserts, and the rollback is written per refusal by hand. The two rollbacks that exist cover a create and never a revise. Fixing one constructor's order would not stop the next field added through set_optional_props.

UNDER MCP: identical. The door runs the same handler in-process, and nothing here depends on the transport.

⑦ NOT DONE: no failing-first test written (triage only, no builds).

⑨ NOT ESTABLISHED:
- which two calls the reporter hit;
- whether the reporter's "already held" was the edge echo or the revision note. The revision note was seen here.
